  "acceptance_rules": [
    "Facility-wide, not a personal preference: open it from the admin's Settings entry (establishment.manage), never from the avatar's Settings modal.",
    "A 'Staff and duties' tab: GET /establishment/staffing after every applied change (and on opening). Show NobodyHolds and NeedsSecondPerson in amber with the message and solo_alternative; never offer to weaken a rule. NotApplicable rows are greyed (the service is not running).",
    "Top: the profile (label, PHC number, effective date, framework and its indicators) and, from GET /msds/profile, what the beds suggest (`note`) with the wards table (emergency wards are not counted). needs_confirmation true: a banner 'Record the category on your PHC licence'. Never change it by yourself: the licence decides, not the bed count.",
    "Services: one row per capability with its state (Available / Preparing / Active / Retiring / Retired), what it needs (`requires`) and its open work (`outstanding`); a service with `implemented` false (none in this release) gets no button.",
    "First setup and every later change are one form: the profile (category from GET /establishment/profiles, pre-tick its `preset`; the person decides each service), the number, the licence from the compliance register (GET /facility/compliance-documents?category=Hospital), the date it took effect, the reason.",
    "Always preview first (POST /establishment/changes/preview) and show it in full: each move in order, its prerequisites (met or missing), the open work of each service being retired, the framework change, the warnings and every `problems` line. Apply is disabled while `allowed` is false.",
    "Apply (POST /establishment/changes) sends the previewed `revision` as expected_revision and the codes of every acknowledgement the person ticked (each shown as a checkbox with its message). VERSION_CONFLICT: someone else changed it; preview again. CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED: tick what details.acknowledgements lists.",
    "Retiring a service with open work: say it plainly ('No new admissions from now on; the 3 admitted patients continue to discharge; their records stay'). Retired only when nothing is open.",
    "Becoming a clinic: inpatient care, the emergency department and the theatre cannot stay Active; the preview says so. Going back to a hospital rechecks every prerequisite (an earlier activation proves nothing).",
    "History: GET /establishment/changes (who, when, why, before and after, the open work at that moment) and GET /msds/category-confirmations (each recorded category with its date). A reversal is a new change."
  ],
  "demo_accounts": "demo_accounts() lists a login per role; sandbox_call runs each case on the DEV server"
}